<title>NEPAL: GOVERNMENT LIST.</title>
<headline>GOVERNMENT LIST.</headline>
<text>
<p>NEPAL GOVERNMENT LIST (970611)</p>
<p> Head of State.....King BIRENDRA</p>
<p> Crown Prince........Prince DIPENDRA Bir Bikram</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p>CABINET (Named 25 Mar 97, See end of list for party</p>
<p>affiliations)</p>
<p>Prime Minister (Sworn in 12 Mar</p>
<p>     97)...........Lokendra Bahadur CHAND (RPP)</p>
<p>(Also minr of Royal Palace Affairs, Defence, Water</p>
<p>Resources, Land Reform and Management, Science and</p>
<p>Technology)</p>
<p>Deputy Prime Minister.....Bam Dev GAUTAM (UML)</p>
<p>(Alsi in charge of the Home (interior) ministry)</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p>MINISTERS:</p>
<p> Commerce...............Buddhi Man TAMANG (RPP)</p>
<p> Defence......See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Finance.............Rabindra Nath SHARMA (RPP)</p>
<p> Foreign Affairs.Prakash Chandra LOHANI (RPP)**</p>
<p>						   (**Resigned 11 June 97)</p>
<p> General Administration..Siddhi Lal SINGH (UML)</p>
<p> Health.............Radha Krishna MAINALI (UML)</p>
<p> Home (Interior).......See Deputy Prime Minster</p>
<p> Housing &amp; Physical Planning..Kamal THAPA (RPP)</p>
<p> Industries...........Keshab Prasad BADAL (UML)</p>
<p> Information &amp; Communications............Jhalnath KHANAL (UML)</p>
<p> Labour....Mukunda NEUPANE (UML)</p>
<p> Land Reform &amp; Management....See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Local Development.....Amrit Kumar BOHARA (UML)</p>
<p> Parliamentary Affairs.....shok Kumar RAI (UML)</p>
<p> Royal Palace Affairs........See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Science &amp; Technology........See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Supplies..........Gajendra Narayan SINGH (NSP)</p>
<p> Tourism, Civil Aviation...............Salim Mian ANSARI (UML)</p>
<p> Water Resources.............See Prime Minister</p>
<p> Women &amp; Social Welfare....Sahana PRADHAN (UML)</p>
<p> Works &amp; Transport..Bharat Mohan ADHIKARY (UML)</p>
<p> Youth...............Bishnu Prasad POUDEL (UML)</p>
<p>			    - - - - - - -</p>
<p>PARTY AFFILIATIONS:</p>
<p>RPP -- Rastriya Prajatantra Party</p>
<p>UML -- United Marxist-Leninist party</p>
<p>NSP -- Nepal Sadbhavana Party</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Central Bank Governor.Satyendra Pyara SHRESTHA</p>
<p>			   - - - - - - -</p>
